### Describe the bug

It looks like swc async wrappers are messing with function.length results ([https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function/length](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function/length)).



### Input code

```typescript
const myFunc = async (one, two, three) => {
    return 'irrelevant'
};

console.log('arity', myFunc.length)
```


### Config

```json
{
  "jsc": {
    "parser": {
      "syntax": "ecmascript",
      "jsx": false
    },
    "target": "es5",
    "loose": false,
    "minify": {
      "compress": false,
      "mangle": false
    }
  },
  "module": {
    "type": "commonjs"
  },
  "minify": false,
  "isModule": true
}
```


### Playground link

https://play.swc.rs/?version=1.2.115&code=H4sIAAAAAAAAAy2MQQqAIBAA775ibxaIHwg79g%2BRRQXbhW0rJPp7HprDzG0S06Gw9%2B2kBAHi0UcnJnSgNw8VQZwhrPAYGAjqKQS2imDDK5Ja8y7GpPHhhr5xnmyUqt26f%2BsbUtYyfzMfQzVrAAAA&config=H4sIAAAAAAAAA0WMSwrDMAxE76K1t93kDj2EcJXg4B8aBWqM714bUrKSmPdmOp3wtHWqrBBdH1o2%2FtJG4hPDa6hGbmoz2jlChiNjPcSWgtdksRTITR2lkMPe1pIvqaoAD%2BJ8xL855lAqn2sFnazVeVcllXyCxjN0lwPet216yfgBCKaI9boAAAA%3D

### Expected behavior

When running the transpiled code (I'm using node to run it), the console.log should print **arity 3**

### Actual behavior

When running the transpiled code (I'm using node to run it), the console.log prints **arity 0**

### Version

1.2.115

